-- title:
--   Cyclicity: a vector generates a cuspidal sub-representation
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, $D$ a subset of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$, $U$ an assignment of a subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ to each ideal of $\mathcal{O}_F$, $\mathrm{gen}$ an assignment of an element of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ to each height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_F$, and $B$ a subset of $\mathbb{A}_F$; all data are packaged as `productionPinsOf F D U gen B`, the carrier pins with the Borel $\sigma$-algebra and Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$, window $D$, central subgroup $\top$, level family $U$, generators $\mathrm{gen}$, the Borel $\sigma$-algebra on $\mathbb{A}_F$ and the additive adelic Haar measure conditioned on $B$. Let $\xi$ be a homomorphism from $\mathbb{A}_F^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, and let $V$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of functions $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)\to\mathbb{C}$ that is a cuspidal sub-representation for $\xi$: $V$ lies in `cuspKFiniteSubmodule` (the span of the continuous functions all of whose right translates are smooth cuspidal automorphic for these pins and $\xi$, and which lie in the archimedean cut submodule of some archimedean type family), and $V$ is stable under right translation by elements of $\ker(\mathrm{glArch})$, under right translation by $\mathrm{rowIsometryInclAt}_0(w,k)$ for every infinite place $w$ and every $k$ in the determinant-one row-isometry subgroup of $F_w$, and under right convolution by factorizable test functions which are archimedean-bi-finite for some type family. Let $\Psi\in V$, and let $C$ be the $\mathbb{C}$-span of all functions of the form $R(gk)\Psi$ and $R(gk)(\Psi * f)$, where $g\in\ker(\mathrm{glArch})$, $k$ lies in the subgroup generated by the images of the archimedean row-isometry inclusions, and $f$ runs over the factorizable, archimedean-bi-finite test functions, with $R(h)\varphi = \varphi(\cdot\, h)$ and $*$ right convolution against the adelic Haar measure. Then $C$ is again a cuspidal sub-representation for $\xi$ in the above sense, $\Psi\in C$, $C\le V$, and if moreover $V$ is a cuspidal constituent (a nonzero cuspidal sub-representation all of whose cuspidal sub-representations contained in it are $\bot$ or $V$) and $\Psi\neq 0$, then $C=V$.
--
--   This is the cyclicity statement for cuspidal sub-representations: the span of the finite-adelic and archimedean-isometry translates of a single vector, together with their right convolutions by archimedean-bi-finite factorizable test functions, is itself stable under all three operations, so by minimality a nonzero vector of a cuspidal constituent generates it. It is used in the results bounding intersections of cuspidal sub-representations with level-invariant and archimedean cut submodules, and in the dichotomy for constituents generated by a principal vector.
